How important is the issue of security of save/bones
contents? As the boss of Hearse, you'd probably be
peeved at a hand built killer bones file, and
presumably with text structures instead of binary
ones, that would be pretty easy.

For folks playing on a shared environment like NAO,
probably security would be important too.

For play on a non-Hearsed personal machine, it
would probably be a non-issue: the player could only
cheat himself or herself.

In the curcumstance that an open format looks like a
good idea despite the security concerns:

1) XML would probably be a useful format, because it
is easy to import/export, and generic code to do so
(that would need additional work) should be widely
available by now, as should the needed programming
skills.

2) Omitting instantiating anything not recognizable
by XML in a bones/save file into the game would
probably be appropriate, though in a rare that case
might cause a "trickery" or other collapse, I
suppose.  Murphy's law is pretty much unbeatable in
the software business.

